<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  The fill of the category-colour preview. An oval with a solid colour the row tints:
  `CategoryDetailFragment` sets `backgroundTintList`, which is what a background is for, rather than
  `setBackgroundColor`, which replaced this whole drawable with a square and turned the round colour preview
  into a colour chip. Stage 8a split the preview in two: this file is the tinted fill, `bg_color_preview` is
  the ring that stays the surface ink whatever colour is chosen, and the ring lives in `android:foreground` so
  a tint cannot reach it.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">
    <!-- White is the tint's multiplicative identity: `backgroundTintList` paints this shape with the chosen
         colour exactly, and any other base colour would darken it. It is named through the design system
         rather than as `@android:color/white` because the night theme re-points the same name, which is what
         keeps the one frame before the first tint lands from showing a bright disc on a dark screen. -->
    <solid android:color="@color/ink_surface" />
</shape>
